  "details": "When avatar scaling, your constraints only get correct from absolute to relative when you **start** scaling. So if you use scaling they'll be noticeably in the wrong position until you tap the scaler again. Though it works as expected for remote users.\n\nI swear this wasn't the case until recently? Or have we all just been unlucky and missed this? *(Also present on the 2022 Open beta)*\n\n![Issue Example](https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/475755800078319629/1149316783203954779/Offset_correction.gif)\n\nIn the above example, the red cube is a child of \"Armature\" and parent constrained to the green cube which is a child of \"Chest\"",
